96 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Samh\345llighet is the  Swedish term that encapsulating the essence of \047sustainability\047 and \047cohesiveness\047\056 \015\n\015\nHow can we innovate the design and material composition of biodegradable bandages to not only enhance their effectiveness in wound care but also minimise environmental impact\054 contributing to create a model for environmentally conscious healthcare solutions that can be rapidly implemented and scaled up\077\015\n\015\nIn response to the escalating demand for sustainable healthcare solutions\054 this material exploration project aims to revolutionise wound care by designing biodegradable bandages\056\015\n\015\nThis project boldly explores the potential of employing more biodegradable materials\054 replacing the prevalent petroleum\055based industrial plastics\056 Can this shift be the antidote to the environmental emergency\054 and when might we witness its widespread adoption\077\015\n\015\nThis endeavour represents a forward\055looking fusion of product design practices and speculative design logic\056 Through the synthesis and application of novel plastics\054 the project not only ponders these pressing questions but also aspires to propel speculative proposals and practices\015\nforward\056\n)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 95 0 R
     /Pg 92 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

